      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as written: **ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily (6400 mg/day)**. The order ID is **ORD-0001**.\n\nBecause the dose is about twice the usual maximum, I added a dose alert to the order. It says you confirmed the dose and requests a pharmacist check before dispensing. Since you didn't give a clinical reason, the note says so. Pharmacy will probably contact you, so it would help to document why you chose this dose.\n\nIf you go ahead with it, these checks would help catch harm early:\n- Kidney function (creatinine) and urine output\n- Signs of GI bleeding, with stomach protection such as a PPI\n- Blood pressure and fluid status\n- Possibly NSAID or salicylate levels if signs of toxicity appear\n\nIf \"1600\" was meant as the daily total, I can cancel this order and enter 400 mg four times daily instead."
      }
